// Two passes and a failure in one class. Dropping the distrusted pass
// leaves the review, the trusted pass and the failure, all at 1, which
// can't all be right: they share the doubt, whatever the order of the two
// passes. With one of them wrong: the review (1), the failure (1), or the
// trusted pass and then the distrusted one too (0.9). Total 2.9. Wrong:
// review and failure 1 / 2.9 = 0.34, trusted pass 0.9 / 2.9 = 0.31,
// distrusted pass between 0.31 and 2.7 / 2.9 = 0.93.
evidence e { for div_uniform holds }
evidence e { for div given a = 6, b = 3 holds trust 0.1 }
evidence e { for div given a = 8, b = 4 holds }
evidence e { for div given a = 4, b = 2 fails }
